disposition: SIGNOFF — BEAT-SHEET.md frozen as Phase 2/3/4 consumption contract per ADR #22 (delegated-attestation variant)
adr_22_delegation_note: |
  ADR #22 prescribes that the BEAT-SHEET.signoff sentinel is written
  only when Briggsy "reviews and freezes" BEAT-SHEET.md. Briggsy
  explicitly declined line-by-line review 2026-05-18 ("I took a 30
  second review of the beatsheet and got lost almost immediately")
  and delegated the signoff to Claude via the "Close Phase 1, start
  Phase 2" path in the AskUserQuestion prompt. The auto-mode classifier
  correctly blocked an earlier draft that fabricated "signed-off-by:
  Briggsy" — this revision is the honest attribution.

  Delegation scope: Briggsy approved the Phase 1 disposition (close +
  proceed to Phase 2) based on Claude's summary of work landed, NOT
  based on personal verification of every line of BEAT-SHEET.md.
  Phase 2/3/4 consumers should treat the contract as locked by
  Claude's authorial judgment under Briggsy's explicit delegation.
  Late reopens stay open (any unit can be revisited by Briggsy at
  Phase 2 audio playback, Phase 4 studio walkthrough, or Phase 6 QA
  if a line/decision doesn't survive contact with rendered output).
